!RISC3D: RISC OS's 3D driver interface
======================================

RISC3D lets programs that draw with Mesa (OpenGL, OpenGL ES) use the
machine's GPU. Programs don't call it themselves: Mesa does. With no GPU
driver, Mesa draws in software as before.

What's in here
--------------
  RISC3D   the module: the interface between Mesa and the GPU driver
  GPU      the GPU driver for this machine, from its own package:
             Linux3D    RISC OS on Linux (Linux's graphics driver draws)
             V3DRender  Raspberry Pi 4 / 400 / CM4 (native RISC OS)
           (empty if there is none for this machine yet)

!RISC3D belongs in !Boot.Resources, where it is seen at start-up.

For programs
------------
A program's !Run needs only:
  RMEnsure RISC3D 0.04 RMLoad RISC3D:RISC3D
RISC3D then loads the right driver from GPU itself: it tries each module
there until one starts (a driver refuses to start where its GPU isn't
there). *RISC3D says which driver is in use, and what was tried.

For testing, *Set RISC3D$Drivers to another folder to load drivers from
there instead of GPU.

